[{"data":1,"prerenderedAt":54},["ShallowReactive",2],{"header-locale:\u002Fen\u002Fcategories\u002FSCSS\u002F":3,"category-page:en:SCSS:1":4,"author-stats:en:full":51},null,{"category":5,"posts":6,"total":49,"totalPages":50},"SCSS",[7,16,24,30,37,43],{"url":8,"title":9,"date":10,"updated":10,"category":5,"tags":11,"description":14,"readingMinutes":15},"\u002Fen\u002Fscss\u002F2025\u002F11\u002F23\u002Fsass-deprecated-import-use-forward-migration\u002F","SCSS Is Deprecating @import?!","2025-11-23 15:32:01",[5,12,13],"Sass","Dart Sass","Sass @import is deprecated and will be removed in Dart Sass 3.0.0. What the deprecation warning means and how to migrate your SCSS to @use and @forward.","4",{"url":17,"title":18,"date":19,"updated":3,"category":5,"tags":20,"description":22,"readingMinutes":23},"\u002Fen\u002Fscss\u002F2019\u002F04\u002F21\u002Fscss-handbook-5-mixin\u002F","SCSS Handbook (5) — mixin","2019-04-21 07:24:30",[5,21],"SCSS Handbook","What an SCSS mixin is and how to use it. Think of a mixin as a library for storing SCSS snippets you use often so you can reuse them across your styles.","2",{"url":25,"title":26,"date":27,"updated":3,"category":5,"tags":28,"description":29,"readingMinutes":23},"\u002Fen\u002Fscss\u002F2019\u002F04\u002F19\u002Fscss-handbook-4-import\u002F","SCSS Handbook (4) — @import","2019-04-19 17:24:30",[5,21],"SCSS provides `@import`, which makes development management way easier when used well.",{"url":31,"title":32,"date":33,"updated":3,"category":5,"tags":34,"description":35,"readingMinutes":36},"\u002Fen\u002Fscss\u002F2019\u002F04\u002F18\u002Fscss-handbook-3-operators\u002F","SCSS Handbook (3) — Operators","2019-04-18 17:24:30",[5,21],"Operators? Like add, subtract, multiply, divide? Yep — SCSS supports operators: add (+), subtract (-), multiply (*), and divide (\u002F).","1",{"url":38,"title":39,"date":40,"updated":3,"category":5,"tags":41,"description":42,"readingMinutes":23},"\u002Fen\u002Fscss\u002F2019\u002F04\u002F17\u002Fscss-handbook-2-variables\u002F","SCSS Handbook (2) — Variables ($)","2019-04-17 12:45:50",[5,21],"From this post on we won't talk about SASS — let's focus on the SCSS basics.",{"url":44,"title":45,"date":46,"updated":3,"category":5,"tags":47,"description":48,"readingMinutes":23},"\u002Fen\u002Fscss\u002F2019\u002F04\u002F16\u002Fscss-handbook-1-intro\u002F","SCSS Handbook (1) — Intro","2019-04-16 20:03:12",[5,21],"The first entry in my SCSS handbook: what SCSS and SASS are, how their syntax differs, and which one to learn, with thanks to a Hexschool SASS guide.",6,1,{"postCount":52,"tagCount":53},1049,1084,1790352042731]